irm. Query \"this week\" maybe. Let''s try searchMail query \"November 2026\" and also check calendar for this week? The user asked about mailboxes only. But \"what needs my attention\" — mail focus.\n\nLet me try searchMail with query \"after:2026-11-01\" — unknown syntax. I''ll try a couple of searches.\n\nAlso worth checking unread/starred. Let me search \"is:unread\" and \"is:starred\".\n\nI''ll do a few searches in parallel.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Only one mailbox, and the newest email is Sep 26, 2026 — over a month before the turn date of Nov 6, 2026. So \"this week\" (Nov 2–6, 2026) has no mail. Hmm. The aggregateInbox returns most recent 15, which are all September. So there''s no mail this week.\n\nWait — maybe the inbox is stale. Let me check: the most recent is Sep 26. So nothing this week. I should report that honestly, and maybe note the most recent items. But maybe I should search for mail in the week window to be sure. searchMail with query — does it support date ranges? Query is a string. Let me try searching for something like \"2026-11\" or just check. Perhaps searchMail supports natural language queries.\n\nLet me do a searchMail for recent mail to confirm. Query \"this week\" maybe. Let''s try searchMail query \"November 2026\" and also check calendar for this week? The user asked about mailboxes only. But \"what needs my attention\" — mail focus.\n\nLet me try searchMail with query \"after:2026-11-01\" — unknown syntax. I''ll try a couple of searches.\n\nAlso worth checking unread/starred. Let me search \"is:unread\" and \"is:starred\".\n\nI''ll do a few searches in parallel."}],"createdAt":1795321938255},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"count":0,"emails":[]},"toolCallId":"call-fd533ac6-f00e-4339-b494-4a9f23d93fa8","toolName":"searchMail","args":{"query":"is:unread","mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134"}},"updatedAt":1795321942520},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state"