:250,"query":"review","timeMax":"2026-12-31T23:59:59Z","timeMin":"2026-09-01T00:00:00Z"}},"updatedAt":1795321945187},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"id":"http://caldav.localhost:5232/ana/personal/tokyo-trip.ics","calendarId":"http://caldav.localhost:5232/ana/personal/","calendarName":"Personal","title":"Tokyo trip","description":"Northbeam Air NB7Q4K. Aozora studio visit on November 11.","start":"2026-11-09","end":"2026-11-15","allDay":true,"recurring":false,"attendees":[],"timeZone":"floating","calendarAccountId":"ef21568e-53a9-597d-bc5c-451f8029a9de","accountEmail":"ana@demo.trymetis.email"},"toolCallId":"call_10df52d7ee634467b4a0472e","toolName":"getEvent","args":{"calendarAccountId":"ef21568e-53a9-597d-bc5c-451f8029a9de","calendarId":"http://caldav.localhost:5232/ana/personal/","eventId":"http://caldav.localhost:5232/ana/personal/tokyo-trip.ics"}},"updatedAt":1795321945188},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1795321945190,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Now assemble the answer. Rebrand-related calendar items:\n\n1. **Aozora rebrand kickoff** — Work calendar, Mon 5 Oct 2026, 10:00–11:30 UTC, Linkroom room. Organizer Raj Mehta. Attendees: Ana accepted, Tomás Ortega accepted, Kenji Watanabe (aozora-ceramics.jp) accepted. Description: \"Agenda: goals, timeline, wordmark directions, packaging constraints.\" This matches exactly \"We agreed to start the rebrand on October 5\" from the kickoff email.\n\n2. **Aozora logo review (internal)** — Work, Thu 1 Oct 2026, 14:00–15:00 UTC, Studio 2. Ana accepted, Tomás **tentative**. Organizer Raj. This is the \"first review\" Raj asked whether Tomás could join — and Tomás answered tentative, not accepted. That''s the concrete answer to Raj''s ask #2: Tomás has not confirmed.\n\n3. Also likely related but not labelled rebrand: **Design review** Thu 8 Oct 15:00–16:00, Work, no attendees listed — the email \"Invitation: Rebrand review @ Thu Oct 8, 2026 15:00 UTC\" from Raj. The calendar event is called \"Design review\" with no attendees. Hmm — that could be the same slot. Worth flagging as likely the rebrand review. I should be careful: same time slot 15:00 on Oct 8, but titled \"Design review\" with no attendees/description. I''ll note it as probable but flagged.\n\n4. No rebrand event after 8 Oct on Work. Nothing upcoming. The next Work items are Monthly studio reviews (2 Nov, 7 Dec). So the rebrand project has no scheduled forward motion.\n\nAlso the Tokyo trip Nov 9–15 mentions \"Aozora studio visit on November 11\" — that''s a rebrand-adjacent item and currently in the past (today Nov 15, trip ends today). That''s a good catch: the rebrand''s next milestone was an Aozora studio visit on 11 Nov during the Tokyo trip. No separate calendar entry for the visit itself — it''s only a line in the trip description.\n\nAlso note: the calendar name is \"Work\" for all these. Also mention that \"Bulk\" calendar has tons of noise; excluded.\n\nLet me also note the discrepancy: the Oct 8 \"Rebrand review\" invitation email exists, but no calendar event titled rebrand review — likely \"Design review\" 15:00 Oct 8 on Work, no attendees. Also worth noting the Oct 8 email invited Ana only (to: ana only) with a join link.\n\nNow, the important synthesis: Raj''s asks — moodboard by Fri 25 Sep; Tomás joining first review — the calendar shows Tomás responded tentative to the 1 Oct logo review. And kickoff Oct 5 happened with Kenji from Aozora attending.\n\nAnswer format: group, concise. Lead with headline. Mention what''s still open.\n\nAlso add: nothing for rebrand after 8 Oct, so if the project is still live, nothing''s booked. Offer to create an event or check the Oct 8 event.\n\nCareful about the \"Design review\" inference — label it as probable.\n\nAlso today is Nov 15 and the Tokyo trip ends today; the studio visit was 11 Nov. If they''re in Tokyo now, that''s live context.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Now assemble the answer. Rebrand-related calendar items:\n\n1. **Aozora rebrand kickoff** — Work calendar, Mon 5 Oct 2026, 10:00–11:30 UTC, Linkroom room. Organizer Raj Mehta. Attendees: Ana accepted, Tomás Ortega accepted, Kenji Watanabe (aozora-ceramics.jp) accepted. Description: \"Agenda: goals, timeline, wordmark directions, packaging constraints.\" This matches exactly \"We agreed to start the rebrand on October 5\" from the kickoff email.\n\n2. **Aozora logo review (internal)** — Work, Thu 1 Oct 2026, 14:00–15:00 UTC, Studio 2. Ana accepted, Tomás **tentative**. Organizer Raj. This is the \"first review\" Raj asked whether Tomás could join — and Tomás answered tentative, not accepted. That''s the concrete answer to Raj''s ask #2: Tomás has not confirmed.\n\n3. Also likely related but not labelled rebrand: **Design review** Thu 8 Oct 15:00–16:00, Work, no attendees listed — the email \"Invitation: Rebrand review @ Thu Oct 8, 2026 15:00 UTC\" from Raj. The calendar event is called \"Design review\" with no attendees. Hmm — that could be the same slot. Worth flagging as likely the rebrand review. I should be careful: same time slot 15:00 on Oct 8, but titled \"Design review\" with no attendees/description. I''ll note it as probable but flagged.\n\n4. No rebrand event after 8 Oct on Work. Nothing upcoming. The next Work items are Monthly studio reviews (2 Nov, 7 Dec). So the rebrand project has no scheduled forward motion.\n\nAlso the Tokyo trip Nov 9–15 mentions \"Aozora studio visit on November 11\" — that''s a rebrand-adjacent item and currently in the past (today Nov 15, trip ends today). That''s a good catch: the rebrand''s next milestone was an Aozora studio visit on 11 Nov during the Tokyo trip. No separate calendar entry for the visit itself — it''s only a line in the trip description.\n\nAlso note: the calendar name is \"Work\" for all these. Also mention that \"Bulk\" calendar has tons of noise; excluded.\n\nLet me also note the discrepancy: the Oct 8 \"Rebrand review\" invitation email exists, but no calendar event titled rebrand review — likely \"Design review\" 15:00 Oct 8 on Work, no attendees. Also worth noting the Oct 8 email invited Ana only (to: ana only) with a join link.\n\nNow, the important synthesis: Raj''s asks — moodboard by Fri 25 Sep; Tomás joining first review — the calendar shows Tomás responded tentative to the 1 Oct logo review. And kickoff Oct 5 happened with Kenji from Aozora attending.\n\nAnswer format: group, concise. Lead with headline. Mention what''s still open.\n\nAlso add: nothing for rebrand after 8 Oct, so if the project is still live, nothing''s booked. Offer to create an event or check the Oct 8 event.\n\nCareful about the \"Design review\" inference — label it as probable.\n\nAlso today is Nov 15 and the Tokyo trip ends today; the studio visit was 11 Nov. If they''re in Tokyo now, that''s live context."}],"createdAt":1795321945315},{"type":"text","text":"**Yes — 3 events on the Work calendar, all in early October, plus one buried in a trip note. Nothing is booked from 8 Oct onward.**\n\n## Work calendar — ana@demo.trymetis.email\n\n**Aozora rebrand kickoff** — Mon 5 Oct 2026, 10:00–11:30 UTC, Linkroom\nOrganiser Raj Mehta; Ana **accepted**, Tomás Ortega **accepted**, Kenji Watanabe (kenji@aozora-ceramics.jp) **accepted**.\n> Agenda: goals, timeline, wordmark directions, packaging constraints.\n\nThis is the 5 October start Raj named in the kickoff email — confirmed on the calendar, with the client in the room.\n\n**Aozora logo review (internal)** — Thu 1 Oct 2026, 14:00–15:00 UTC, Studio 2\nOrganiser Raj Mehta; Ana **accepted**, Tomás Ortega **tentative**.\n\nThis is almost certainly the \"first review\" from Raj''s email — and it answers his second ask directly: **Tomás never confirmed, he only answered tentative.** So Raj''s question (\"confirm whether Tomás can join\") was never really settled.\n\n**Design review** — Thu 8 Oct 2026, 15:00–16:00 UTC, Studio 2 — *probable, not certain*\nSame slot as the *Invitation: Rebrand review @ Thu Oct 8 15:00 UTC* email in your inbox, but this calendar entry is titled \"Design review\" with no attendees and no description. I''d treat the match as likely rather than proven.\n\n## Personal calendar\n**Tokyo trip** — all-day 9–15 Nov 2026. Description: *\"Northbeam Air NB7Q4K. Aozora studio visit on November 11.\"*\n\nThat closes the loop from earlier: the flight was taken, and the rebrand''s next real-world step — an Aozora studio visit on 11 Nov — was tracked only as a line in a trip note, not as its own event. It''s now behind you; the trip ends today.\n\n## What this adds up to\nThe rebrand has a clean trail through 8 Oct — kickoff held, client attended, agenda set — and then stops. No review, no follow-up, nothing on the calendar for the rest of November or December (only the recurring Monthly studio review). Combined with Raj''s moodboard request from 21 Sep still sitting without a reply in the inbox and Tomás only ever tentative, the pattern is a project that started properly and then went quiet on scheduling.\n\nWant me to look at the 8 Oct *Design review* event in full to confirm it''s the rebrand review, or check Sent for your reply to Raj before anything else?","createdAt":1795321945315}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**Yes — 3 events on the Work calendar, all in early October, plus one buried in a trip note. Nothing is booked from 8 Oct onward.**\n\n## Work calendar — ana@demo.trymetis.email\n\n**Aozora rebrand kickoff** — Mon 5 Oct 2026, 10:00–11:30 UTC, Linkroom\nOrganiser Raj Mehta; Ana **accepted**, Tomás Ortega **accepted**, Kenji Watanabe (kenji@aozora-ceramics.jp) **accepted**.\n> Agenda: goals, timeline, wordmark directions, packaging constraints.\n\nThis is the 5 October start Raj named in the kickoff email — confirmed on the calendar, with the client in the room.\n\n**Aozora logo review (internal)** — Thu 1 Oct 2026, 14:00–15:00 UTC, Studio 2\nOrganiser Raj Mehta; Ana **accepted**, Tomás Ortega **tentative**.\n\nThis is almost certainly the \"first review\" from Raj''s email — and it answers his second ask directly: **Tomás never confirmed, he only answered tentative.** So Raj''s question (\"confirm whether Tomás can join\") was never really settled.\n\n**Design review** — Thu 8 Oct 2026, 15:00–16:00 UTC, Studio 2 — *probable, not certain*\nSame slot as the *Invitation: Rebrand review @ Thu Oct 8 15:00 UTC* email in your inbox, but this calendar entry is titled \"Design review\" with no attendees and no description. I''d treat the match as likely rather than proven.\n\n## Personal calendar\n**Tokyo trip** — all-day 9–15 Nov 2026. Description: *\"Northbeam Air NB7Q4K. Aozora studio visit on November 11.\"*\n\nThat closes the loop from earlier: the flight was taken, and the rebrand''s next real-world step — an Aozora studio visit on 11 Nov — was tracked only as a line in a trip note, not as its own event. It''s now behind you; the trip ends today.\n\n## What this adds up to\nThe rebrand has a clean trail through 8 Oct — kickoff held, client attended, agenda set — and then stops. No review, no follow-up, nothing on the calendar for the rest of November or December (only the recurring Monthly studio review). Combined with Raj''s moodboard request from 21 Sep still sitting without a reply in the inbox and Tomás only ever tentative, the pattern is a project that started properly and then went quiet on scheduling.\n\nWant me to look at the 8 Oct *Design review* event in full to confirm it''s the rebrand review, or check Sent for your reply to Raj before anything else?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-22T04:32:22.734Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
