view — relevant since packaging is deliverable #3 and the brief''s \"packaging constraints\" was a kickoff agenda item.\n\nI should mention the Edge cases calendar items are test/noise entries — and clarify: \"Ten year all-day event\" spans the whole day technically, plus \"Daily forever\" duplicates the standup.\n\nPresent concisely."}],"createdAt":1795321949054},{"type":"text","text":"**Thursday 8 October 2026 — four working events around the review, on two calendars.**\n\nAll times UTC, all on ana@demo.trymetis.email.\n\n| Time | Event | Calendar | Where |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 09:00–09:15 | Daily standup | Work | Linkroom |\n| 10:00–13:00 | **Workshop: packaging prototypes** | Work | Studio 2 |\n| 13:00–13:30 | Print vendor call (Pune) | Work | Linkroom |\n| 15:00–16:00 | **Design review** (= the rebrand review) | Work | Studio 2 |\n\n**The one that matters:** the packaging workshop runs 10:00–13:00 the same day, **in the same room as the review**, with Raj and Priya. Packaging is deliverable three in the brief and \"packaging constraints\" was on the kickoff agenda — so the review was stacked on top of a packaging session, not a clean wordmark-only day. Worth keeping in mind given the brief asks for three wordmark options *at* that review.\n\n**Tight, but no clash:** the print vendor call starts exactly as the workshop ends — back-to-back, 30 minutes, with Priya. Then a clear 90-minute gap before 15:00.\n\n**Also on the day, from your \"Edge cases\" calendar:** a *Ten year all-day event* (spans 1 Jan 2026 → 1 Jan 2036, so it technically covers every day including this one) and *Daily forever* at 09:00–09:15, which duplicates the standup. Both look like test entries rather than real commitments.\n\nOne loose thread: the review block runs to 16:00, but Raj''s invitation said 15:00–**15:45**. The calendar gives it a full hour; the invite gave it 45 minutes.","createdAt":1795321949054}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-c