INR 450) — but \"lately\" relative to 15 Nov means the last ~6 weeks: nothing since 25 Sep. So no money out of that account in ~7 weeks according to alerts.\n\nAmounts are nominal — small (450, 980, 1,250, 1,260, 2,150, 2,340, 2,760, 3,100, 3,480, 4,200, 6,300, 7,850, 12,500). These don''t look like the user''s actual spend profile (a rebrand budget of JPY 1.85M etc.). But whatever.\n\nAlso there''s the Hindi-language debit on 19 Jul INR 3,100 — which only surfaced via \"INR\" search, not \"debited\". That''s an important note: notification language varies, so English keyword searches would miss it. I found it.\n\nAlso: no amounts in the emails — just subjects. Bodies aren''t fetched for these. Should I have read the bodies? I only read three bodies (shipping ones). The debit emails have empty snippets and I haven''t read the body — the body would say the merchant. That''s a significant gap: knowing *what* the money went to. Let me consider reading a couple of the recent debit bodies. Actually I can''t call tools now — \"This is your final step... Do not call any more tools.\" Wait, that instruction was for the previous message. Now this is a new turn with the same instruction? The system prompt says \"This is your final step for this message\" — that applies to each message. But I''ve already called tools this turn. Hmm, the instruction came at the end of the system prompt for the current message too. Actually the system prompt includes that block always. I''ve been calling tools. The safe interpretation: I should wrap up now.\n\nI should be candid that the debit alerts carry amounts in the subject but I did not open their bodies to see the merchant — so I can say what moved, not who took it. That''s honest.\n\nAlso the important caveat: the Konkan Bank debit alerts look sporadic (14 in ~2 years) — that''s far too few for a real account, so these are likely only a subset of notifications, e.g. large/unusual ones, or a partial mailbox. So \"no money out lately\" is a statement about *alerts in your mail*, not about your account balance.\n\nOther recurring charges visible: Ledgerline monthly invoices (monthly, latest 1 Sep LL-2025111), Linkroom Pro renewal coming 3 Oct, Codeyard Team renewed 14 Feb, Voltaro Energy bills (Sep 8).\n\nLet me structure the answer:\n\nHeadline: Nothing has left a/c **4821 in the last seven weeks — newest debit alert is 25 Sep.\n\nRecent debits (2026): table.\n- Fri 25 Sep — INR 1,250.00\n- Sat 12 Sep — INR 450.00\n- Sun 2 Aug — INR 2,760.00\n- Sun 19 Jul — INR 3,100.00 (Hindi subject — would have been missed by English search)\n- Mon 8 Jun — INR 980.00\n- Fri 17 Apr — INR 6,300.00\n\nThen: the 6,300 out / 6,300 back in — 17 Apr debit, 29 Apr credit, same amount, 12 days. Looks like a reversal/refund, and it''s the only credit in the whole record.\n\nThen: weaknesses — amounts only, no merchant (bodies not opened); alerts are sparse; and a recurring-billing layer whose charges do NOT appear in the bank alerts at all: Ledgerline monthly invoices every month, latest 1 Sep; Linkroom Pro renews 3 Oct; Voltaro Energy bills. If those are paid from **4821, the alerts aren''t capturing them — meaning the alert stream isn''t a complete picture.\n\nAlso note the security-adjacent item: \"New device registered for mobile banking\" 22 May 2026.\n\nI should not overclaim. Offer next steps: open the recent debit bodies for merchant names; or check the statement PDF attachments in Drive.\n\nLet me be honest about tool limits: I searched mail; statements may exist as attachments I haven''t opened.\n\nAlso note scanning date window: \"lately\" — I''ll use the last ~2 months (mid-Sep to 15 Nov) as \"lately\" and give the year for context.\n\nThe Jun 8 2026 and Apr 17 for context. Fine.\n\nOne more caveat: the mailbox is ana@demo.trymetis.email — single mailbox, no other mailboxes to check? I didn''t call listMailboxes. I should say results are from this mailbox only. Actually, the instruction says call listMailboxes before acting on a mailbox you cannot name. I named it from results. I''ll note I searched every mailbox by default and only this one surfaced results — actually searchMail searches every mailbox by default, and all results were from ana@. So I can say that.\n\nWrite it.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"I''ve done a lot of searching. Time to answer. I should be honest about what I found: Konkan Bank a/c **4821 debit alerts, most recent 25 Sep 2026 (INR 1,250) and 12 Sep (INR 450) — but \"lately\" relative to 15 Nov means the last ~6 weeks: nothing since 25 Sep. So no money out of that account in ~7 weeks according to alerts.\n\nAmounts are nominal — small (450, 980, 1,250, 1,260, 2,150, 2,340, 2,760, 3,100, 3,480, 4,200, 6,300, 7,850, 12,500). These don''t look like the user''s actual spend profile (a rebrand budget of JPY 1.85M etc.). But whatever.\n\nAlso there''s the Hindi-language debit on 19 Jul INR 3,100 — which only surfaced via \"INR\" search, not \"debited\". That''s an important note: notification language varies, so English keyword searches would miss it. I found it.\n\nAlso: no amounts in the emails — just subjects. Bodies aren''t fetched for these. Should I have read the bodies? I only read three bodies (shipping ones). The debit emails have empty snippets and I haven''t read the body — the body would say the merchant. That''s a significant gap: knowing *what* the money went to. Let me consider reading a couple of the recent debit bodies. Actually I can''t call tools now — \"This is your final step... Do not call any more tools.\" Wait, that instruction was for the previous message. Now this is a new turn with the same instruction? The system prompt says \"This is your final step for this message\" — that applies to each message. But I''ve already called tools this turn. Hmm, the instruction came at the end of the system prompt for the current message too. Actually the system prompt includes that block always. I''ve been calling tools. The safe interpretation: I should wrap up now.\n\nI should be candid that the debit alerts carry amounts in the subject but I did not open their bodies to see the merchant — so I can say what moved, not who took it. That''s honest.\n\nAlso the important caveat: the Konkan Bank debit alerts look sporadic (14 in ~2 years) — that''s far too few for a real account, so these are likely only a subset of notifications, e.g. large/unusual ones, or a partial mailbox. So \"no money out lately\" is a statement about *alerts in your mail*, not about your account balance.\n\nOther recurring charges visible: Ledgerline monthly invoices (monthly, latest 1 Sep LL-2025111), Linkroom Pro renewal coming 3 Oct, Codeyard Team renewed 14 Feb, Voltaro Energy bills (Sep 8).\n\nLet me structure the answer:\n\nHeadline: Nothing has left a/c **4821 in the last seven weeks — newest debit alert is 25 Sep.\n\nRecent debits (2026): table.\n- Fri 25 Sep — INR 1,250.00\n- Sat 12 Sep — INR 450.00\n- Sun 2 Aug — INR 2,760.00\n- Sun 19 Jul — INR 3,100.00 (Hindi subject — would have been missed by English search)\n- Mon 8 Jun — INR 980.00\n- Fri 17 Apr — INR 6,300.00\n\nThen: the 6,300 out / 6,300 back in — 17 Apr debit, 29 Apr credit, same amount, 12 days. Looks like a reversal/refund, and it''s the only credit in the whole record.\n\nThen: weaknesses — amounts only, no merchant (bodies not opened); alerts are sparse; and a recurring-billing layer whose charges do NOT appear in the bank alerts at all: Ledgerline monthly invoices every month, latest 1 Sep; Linkroom Pro renews 3 Oct; Voltaro Energy bills. If those are paid from **4821, the alerts aren''t capturing them — meaning the alert stream isn''t a complete picture.\n\nAlso note the security-adjacent item: \"New device registered for mobile banking\" 22 May 2026.\n\nI should not overclaim. Offer next steps: open the recent debit bodies for merchant names; or check the statement PDF attachments in Drive.\n\nLet me be honest about tool limits: I searched mail; statements may exist as attachments I haven''t opened.\n\nAlso note scanning date window: \"lately\" — I''ll use the last ~2 months (mid-Sep to 15 Nov) as \"lately\" and give the year for context.\n\nThe Jun 8 2026 and Apr 17 for context. Fine.\n\nOne more caveat: the mailbox is ana@demo.trymetis.email — single mailbox, no other mailboxes to check? I didn''t call listMailboxes. I should say results are from this mailbox only. Actually, the instruction says call listMailboxes before acting on a mailbox you cannot name. I named it from results. I''ll note I searched every mailbox by default and only this one surfaced results — actually searchMail searches every mailbox by default, and all results were from ana@. So I can say that.\n\nWrite it."}],"createdAt":1795321979657},{"type":"text","text":"**No — nothing has left a/c \\*\\*4821 in about seven weeks.** The newest debit alert is **25 September**, and the mailbox is quiet on money since then.\n\nPrices below are as they appear in the alert subjects, from ana@demo.trymetis.email (the only mailbox that returned any bank mail when I searched all of them).\n\n## Debits in the last stretch\n\n| Date | Amount | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fri 25 Sep 2026 | INR 1,250.00 | newest of the lot |\n| Sat 12 Sep 2026 | INR 450.00 | |\n| Sun 2 Aug 2026 | INR 2,760.00 | |\n| Sun 19 Jul 2026 | INR 3,100.00 | Hindi subject — see below |\n| Mon 8 Jun 2026 | INR 980.00 | |\n| Fri 17 Apr 2026 | INR 6,300.00 | came back — see below |\n\nFor scale, the whole 21-month record holds 14 debits, the largest INR 12,500 (Feb 2025). Nothing exotic.\n\n## Two things worth your attention\n\n**The only credit in the entire record mirrors a debit.** INR 6,300.00 left on 17 Apr 2026 and came back on 29 Apr 2026 — same amount, twelve days apart. That reads like a reversal or failed transaction rather than income, and it''s the sole credit line anywhere in your mail.\n\n**One debit would have been invisible to a normal search.** The 19 Jul 2026 entry is written in Hindi: *खाता \\*\\*4821 से INR 3,100.00 डेबिट*. Searching \"debited\" in English does not find it; only \"INR\" does. If you ever check this yourself, search the currency, not the verb.\n\n## What this answer can''t tell you\n\n**Who took the money.** Every alert carries the amount in the subject, not the merchant. I didn''t open the bodies — so I can say what moved and when, but not to whom.\n\n**Whether it''s the full picture — and I doubt it is.** Your recurring billing never shows up here: **Ledgerline** invoices you monthly with no gaps (latest LL-2025111, 1 Sep), **Linkroom Pro** renews 3 Oct, **Voltaro Energy** bills every quarter, **Codeyard Team** renewed 14 Feb. If any of those draw on \\*\\*4821, then the debit alerts are not a complete ledger of that account — 14 alerts across two years is far too few for real spending. That would make \"no money out lately\" a statement about *notifications*, not about your balance.\n\nAlso sitting in the record, unrelated to spending but not unrelated to money: *\"New device registered for mobile banking\"* on 22 May 2026. Nothing in your mail confirms whether you did that.\n\n## What I''d do next\n\n- Open the 25 Sep and 12 Sep alert bodies to name the merchants — those are the two you''d want to recognise.\n- Or I could check whether the Konkan Bank statement PDFs (the Jun–Aug 2026 one, 1 Sep) landed in your Drive, which would give the merchants in one shot.\n\nSay which and I''ll go.","createdAt":1795321979657}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**No — nothing has left a/c \\*\\*4821 in about seven weeks.** The newest debit alert is **25 September**, and the mailbox is quiet on money since then.\n\nPrices below are as they appear in the alert subjects, from ana@demo.trymetis.email (the only mailbox that returned any bank mail when I searched all of them).\n\n## Debits in the last stretch\n\n| Date | Amount | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fri 25 Sep 2026 | INR 1,250.00 | newest of the lot |\n| Sat 12 Sep 2026 | INR 450.00 | |\n| Sun 2 Aug 2026 | INR 2,760.00 | |\n| Sun 19 Jul 2026 | INR 3,100.00 | Hindi subject — see below |\n| Mon 8 Jun 2026 | INR 980.00 | |\n| Fri 17 Apr 2026 | INR 6,300.00 | came back — see below |\n\nFor scale, the whole 21-month record holds 14 debits, the largest INR 12,500 (Feb 2025). Nothing exotic.\n\n## Two things worth your attention\n\n**The only credit in the entire record mirrors a debit.** INR 6,300.00 left on 17 Apr 2026 and came back on 29 Apr 2026 — same amount, twelve days apart. That reads like a reversal or failed transaction rather than income, and it''s the sole credit line anywhere in your mail.\n\n**One debit would have been invisible to a normal search.** The 19 Jul 2026 entry is written in Hindi: *खाता \\*\\*4821 से INR 3,100.00 डेबिट*. Searching \"debited\" in English does not find it; only \"INR\" does. If you ever check this yourself, search the currency, not the verb.\n\n## What this answer can''t tell you\n\n**Who took the money.** Every alert carries the amount in the subject, not the merchant. I didn''t open the bodies — so I can say what moved and when, but not to whom.\n\n**Whether it''s the full picture — and I doubt it is.** Your recurring billing never shows up here: **Ledgerline** invoices you monthly with no gaps (latest LL-2025111, 1 Sep), **Linkroom Pro** renews 3 Oct, **Voltaro Energy** bills every quarter, **Codeyard Team** renewed 14 Feb. If any of those draw on \\*\\*4821, then the debit alerts are not a complete ledger of that account — 14 alerts across two years is far too few for real spending. That would make \"no money out lately\" a statement about *notifications*, not about your balance.\n\nAlso sitting in the record, unrelated to spending but not unrelated to money: *\"New device registered for mobile banking\"* on 22 May 2026. Nothing in your mail confirms whether you did that.\n\n## What I''d do next\n\n- Open the 25 Sep and 12 Sep alert bodies to name the merchants — those are the two you''d want to recognise.\n- Or I could check whether the Konkan Bank statement PDFs (the Jun–Aug 2026 one, 1 Sep) landed in your Drive, which would give the merchants in one shot.\n\nSay which and I''ll go."}','assistant','v2','2026-11-22T04:32:34.330Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
