 Fri 20 Nov 2026) real calendar: only Daily standup 09:00 UTC each weekday, and Weekly 1:1 Ana / Raj Tue 17 Nov 10:00–10:30 UTC. Personal calendar: nothing (Tokyo trip all-day ended 15 Nov — today it ends! Tokyo trip Nov 9–15, meaning she returns today).\n- Notably: \"Weekly 1:1 Ana / Raj\" has attendee ana@demo.trymetis.email only, and location linkroom.app/r/ana-raj — but Raj is NOT a workspace member. That''s consistent: he''s external.\n- Ahead: Monthly studio review Mon 7 Dec 14:00–15:00 UTC, Studio 1, with raj@, tomas@, priya@ on the invite. Aozora launch? Not on the calendar at all. That''s a gap: the \"Venue for the Aozora launch\" thread (Sep 8-9, starred, with Mira Costa) and \"Harbour Hall hold\" sent by Ana — but no launch event on any calendar. That''s a real to-do: the launch is nowhere on the calendar.\n- Tokyo trip ends today (15 Nov) — return travel day. Mail silent since 26 Sep, consistent with being away? But the trip was 9–15 Nov.\n\nSo the prioritized to-do list for this week, grounded in evidence:\n\nP1 — Today/this week, has a date attached:\n1. Raj 1:1 Tue 17 Nov 10:00 UTC — only real meeting this week; prep. But is the 1:1 in question? Actually with an external \"Raj\" (Raj Mehta at aozora? raj@demo.trymetis.email is an internal-looking domain though — demo.trymetis.email, same domain as Ana. So Raj may be a colleague on the same mail domain but not a workspace member. Interesting: the members list has only Ana, but calendar has raj@demo.trymetis.email, tomas@, priya@ — same domain. So the workspace has one member but colleagues share the mail domain. That''s a notable discrepancy worth flagging: workspace ≠ domain.\n\nP1 items:\n1. **Aozora launch is not on any calendar.** Venue thread live as of 9 Sep (Mira Costa reply, starred; you sent \"Harbour Hall hold\" 9 Sep 12:10). No launch event in any visible calendar through 31 Dec. The signed proposal exists (drive: Proposal - signed.pdf, 789 B). Highest-value item: pick the date, get Harbour Hall confirmed, put it on the calendar.\n2. **Kestrel/Linkroom renewals** — Linkroom Pro renews 3 October (passed); Voltaro bill; Ledgerline invoices LL-2025111; Konkan statements. Finance follow-ups: \"Receipts for September\" from Sam (16 Sep) — unanswered? Unknown but likely.\n3. **Codeyard review request open since 11 Sep** — \"Review requested: Aozora case study (#63)\"; plus Dependabot 4 security updates (14 Sep) unaddressed in a stale repo. \n4. **Mailbox hygiene, cheap and high-leverage**: 228 unread that are all fixtures — mark read/archive so real unread becomes meaningful; label the 75 newsletters.\n5. **Drives**: establish which of the 7 mounts is canonical; the four same-tree mounts risk divergence. Ask: consolidate to one mount, or keep and document.\n6. **Silence check**: nothing in inbox since 26 Sep — confirm forwarding/filters aren''t broken, since you''ve been away (Tokyo 9–15 Nov). This is a genuine risk: 6-7 weeks with zero real mail is suspicious if the studio is active. Also Mailbox has no workflow? Could check workflows, but not asked.\n\nAlso: the Tokyo trip ended today — so first item may be \"you land today\" (Nov 9–15 all-day, ends today). So this week is a re-entry week.\n\nI should be careful not to invent deadlines. Priorities should reflect: (a) dated commitments this week, (b) things that are overdue with dates in mail, (c) hygiene.\n\nRanking by consequence, honestly:\nP1 (this week, dated):\n- Tue 17 Nov 10:00 UTC — 1:1 with Raj (only non-recurring-standing event). Prep: the Aozora rebrand threads are all read but there are unanswered? Raj''s last mails: Rebrand kickoff (Sep 21), Rebrand review invite (Sep 24). Nothing since.\n- Daily standups 09:00 — attending them means you''re back at work, and any open loops surface there.\n\nP1 (undated but highest consequence):\n- Aozora launch: no date, no calendar entry, venue hold placed 9 Sep that has presumably expired after 2+ months. Needs a decision first — this is the single biggest gap.\n\nP2:\n- Codeyard: Aozora case study review #63 (blocked since 11 Sep), Dependabot security updates.\n- Finance: review September receipts from Sam, Ledgerline invoice LL-2025111, check Konkan debits vs expenses.tsv; Linkroom renews Oct 3 (already charged?).\n\nP3 (hygiene, low effort, high clarity):\n- Mark/archive the 228 fixture unreads; label 75 newsletters; verify mail flow (why nothing since 26 Sep).\n\nI should present as a prioritized list with reasons and evidence, note what''s calendar-verified vs inferred, and end with an offer of concrete actions (I can do: label, archive? Actually archive tool not loaded — I could search. Don''t promise beyond tools? I can offer to draft, label, create calendar event, etc.)\n\nAlso mention uncertainty: I did not read email bodies, so I can''t confirm whether items like the Codeyard review were handled off-mail. Be explicit.\n\nAlso flag the domain-vs-member discrepancy: colleagues @demo.trymetis.email invited to the Dec 7 review but not workspace members — so \"invite Priya/Raj/Tomás to the workspace\" is an optional item.\n\nLet me check: which items would be P1 if strictly \"this week\"? Only the 1:1 and standups. The Aozora launch has no date — flag as \"the one thing that has no date at all\".\n\nStructure:\n- One-line headline.\n- \"The week actually on your calendar\" (verified): 6 events, 5 standups + 1 one-to-one. Nothing on Personal.\n- Then P1/P2/P3 list.\n- Then caveats.\n\nKeep tight and concrete. About 400-600 words.\n\nNote Tokyo trip: all-day 9–15 Nov on Personal, ends today — so today is the return day. Good context for \"re-entry week\".\n\nDeadline calls: I shouldn''t claim the Harbour Hall hold expired — unknown; say \"placed 9 Sep, eight weeks ago — worth confirming it''s still held.\"\n\nLet me write.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Key facts:\n- This week (Mon 16 – Fri 20 Nov 2026) real calendar: only Daily standup 09:00 UTC each weekday, and Weekly 1:1 Ana / Raj Tue 17 Nov 10:00–10:30 UTC