l; Ledgerline invoices LL-2025111; Konkan statements. Finance follow-ups: \"Receipts for September\" from Sam (16 Sep) — unanswered? Unknown but likely.\n3. **Codeyard review request open since 11 Sep** — \"Review requested: Aozora case study (#63)\"; plus Dependabot 4 security updates (14 Sep) unaddressed in a stale repo. \n4. **Mailbox hygiene, cheap and high-leverage**: 228 unread that are all fixtures — mark read/archive so real unread becomes meaningful; label the 75 newsletters.\n5. **Drives**: establish which of the 7 mounts is canonical; the four same-tree mounts risk divergence. Ask: consolidate to one mount, or keep and document.\n6. **Silence check**: nothing in inbox since 26 Sep — confirm forwarding/filters aren''t broken, since you''ve been away (Tokyo 9–15 Nov). This is a genuine risk: 6-7 weeks with zero real mail is suspicious if the studio is active. Also Mailbox has no workflow? Could check workflows, but not asked.\n\nAlso: the Tokyo trip ended today — so first item may be \"you land today\" (Nov 9–15 all-day, ends today). So this week is a re-entry week.\n\nI should be careful not to invent deadlines. Priorities should reflect: (a) dated commitments this week, (b) things that are overdue with dates in mail, (c) hygiene.\n\nRanking by consequence, honestly:\nP1 (this week, dated):\n- Tue 17 Nov 10:00 UTC — 1:1 with Raj (only non-recurring-standing event). Prep: the Aozora rebrand threads are all read but there are unanswered? Raj''s last mails: Rebrand kickoff (Sep 21), Rebrand review invite (Sep 24). Nothing since.\n- Daily standups 09:00 — attending them means you''re back at work, and any open loops surface there.\n\nP1 (undated but highest consequence):\n- Aozora launch: no date, no calendar entry, venue hold placed 9 Sep that has presumably expired after 2+ months. Needs a decision first — this is the single biggest gap.\n\nP2:\n- Codeyard: Aozora case study review #63 (blocked since 11 Sep), Dependabot security updates.\n- Finance: review September receipts from Sam, Ledgerline invoice LL-2025111, check Konkan debits vs expenses.tsv; Linkroom renews Oct 3 (already charged?).\n\nP3 (hygiene, low effort, high clarity):\n- Mark/archive the 228 fixture unreads; label 75 newsletters; verify mail flow (why nothing since 26 Sep).\n\nI should present as a prioritized list with reasons and evidence, note what''s calendar-verified vs inferred, and end with an offer of concrete actions (I can do: label, archive? Actually archive tool not loaded — I could search. Don''t promise beyond tools? I can offer to draft, label, create calendar event, etc.)\n\nAlso mention uncertainty: I did not read email bodies, so I can''t confirm whether items like the Codeyard review were handled off-mail. Be explicit.\n\nAlso flag the domain-vs-member discrepancy: colleagues @demo.trymetis.email invited to the Dec 7 review but not workspace members — so \"invite Priya/Raj/Tomás to the workspace\" is an optional item.\n\nLet me check: which items would be P1 if strictly \"this week\"? Only the 1:1 and standups. The Aozora launch has no date — flag as \"the one thing that has no date at all\".\n\nStructure:\n- One-line headline.\n- \"The week actually on your calendar\" (verified): 6 events, 5 standups + 1 one-to-one. Nothing on Personal.\n- Then P1/P2/P3 list.\n- Then caveats.\n\nKeep tight and concrete. About 400-600 words.\n\nNote Tokyo trip: all-day 9–15 Nov on Personal, ends today — so today is the return day. Good context for \"re-entry week\".\n\nDeadline calls: I shouldn''t claim the Harbour Hall hold expired — unknown; say \"placed 9 Sep, eight weeks ago — worth confirming it''s still held.\"\n\nLet me write."}],"createdAt":1795321987105},{"type":"text","text":"**One line: your calendar has almost nothing this week — 5 standups and one 1:1 — and the biggest open item, the Aozora launch, has no date anywhere.**\n\n## What''s actually booked (Mon 16 – Sun 22 Nov 2026)\n\n| When (UTC) | What | Calendar |\n|---|---|---|\n| Mon–Fri 09:00–09:15 | Daily standup | Work |\n| **Tue 17, 10:00–10:30** | **Weekly 1:1 Ana / Raj** | Work |\n| — | *nothing else* | Personal is empty |\n\nToday is the last day of your **Tokyo trip** (all-day, 9–15 Nov), so this is a re-entry week: one real meeting, five standups.\n\n---\n\n## P1 — Decide now, because nothing is forcing it\n\n**1. Aozora launch: no date, no venue confirmation, no calendar entry.**\nThe venue thread ran 8–9 Sep — you asked, Mira Costa replied, you sent *\"Harbour Hall hold\"* on 9 Sep at 12:10. Eight weeks later there is still **no launch event in any of the four visible calendars through 31 December.** A signed proposal exists (`Clients/Aozora Ceramics/Proposal - signed.pdf`, 789 B), so this is a live, contracted project with a deadline nobody has written down. First job: fix the date, then confirm the Harbour Hall hold still stands.\n\n**2. Confirm the 1:1 with Raj on Tuesday still makes sense.** It''s the only non-recurring commitment in your week, and the Aozora rebrand threads (logo shortlist, packaging, Arabic proofs) have been silent since late September — that''s the agenda: what happened while the thread went quiet.\n\n## P2 — Overdue, with dates that have already passed\n\n**3. Codeyard review request #63 — *[fernhill/website] Review requested: Aozora case study*, open since 11 Sep.** Nobody can merge it without you.\n\n**4. Dependabot: 4 security updates** on `fernhill/website`, from 14 Sep. Two months on a stale branch.\n\n**5. Money: settle September.** Sam''s *\"Receipts for September\"* (16 Sep), Ledgerline invoice `LL-2025111`, and a run of Konkan debits to reconcile against `Finance/2025/expenses.tsv`. Also check whether Linkroom''s Pro renewal actually hit on 3 October as it warned.\n\n## P3 — Hygiene that makes the rest trustworthy (30 minutes, once)\n\n**6. Do something with the 228 fake unread emails.** Until they''re gone, your unread badge is noise and you''ll never spot a real one.\n\n**7. Label the 75 newsletters.** Then `newsletter` stops 56 Kestrel editions from crowding anything that matters.\n\n**8. Check why mail has been silent since 26 September.** Seven weeks with zero real arrivals while a studio is actively billing clients is either a genuine lull or a broken filter. Worth ten minutes on filters and forwarding — this one is a *suspicion*, not a finding.\n\n---\n\n## Three things I want to be straight about\n\n- **I read no email bodies.** These items come from subjects, dates and threads. I can''t see whether #63 was reviewed inside Codeyard''s UI, or whether Sam''s receipts were paid by other means. Treat P2 as \"verify,\" not \"certainly undone.\"\n- **Your calendar is buried under fixtures.** Asking for \"this week\" across all calendars returned 100 events and nearly all were `Bulk NNN` filler on a **Bulk** calendar that''s marked *primary*, plus a **\"Daily forever\"** recurrence on Edge cases. I excluded both to find your six real events. Deleting those two calendars would make every future calendar question honest.\n- **Your colleagues aren''t in this workspace, but they''re on your domain.** `raj@`, `tomas@`, `priya@demo.trymetis.email` are invited to the **Monthly studio review on Mon 7 December, 14:00–15:00 UTC, Studio 1** — yet `listWorkspaceMembers` returns only you. So the workspace has one member while the studio works over the same domain.\n\n**Where I''d start:** block 30 minutes today to pick the Aozora launch date and email Mira about Harbour Hall — everything else can wait for Tuesday.\n\nWant me to draft that venue email to Mira Costa, or create the launch event once you''ve chosen a date? I can also clear the 228 fixtures and apply the newsletter label in two actions.","createdAt":1795321987105}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**One line: your calendar has almost nothing this week — 5 standups and one 1:1 — and the biggest open item, the Aozora launch, has no date anywhere.**\n\n## What''s actually booked (Mon 16 – Sun 22 Nov 2026)\n\n| When (UTC) | What | Calendar |\n|---|---|---|\n| Mon–Fri 09:00–09:15 | Daily standup | Work |\n| **Tue 17, 10:00–10:30** | **Weekly 1:1 Ana / Raj** | Work |\n| — | *nothing else* | Personal is empty |\n\nToday is the last day of your **Tokyo trip** (all-day, 9–15 Nov), so this is a re-entry week: one real meeting, five standups.\n\n---\n\n## P1 — Decide now, because nothing is forcing it\n\n**1. Aozora launch: no date, no venue confirmation, no calendar entry.**\nThe venue thread ran 8–9 Sep — you asked, Mira Costa replied, you sent *\"Harbour Hall hold\"* on 9 Sep at 12:10. Eight weeks later there is still **no launch event in any of the four visible calendars through 31 December.** A signed proposal exists (`Clients/Aozora Ceramics/Proposal - signed.pdf`, 789 B), so this is a live, contracted project with a deadline nobody has written down. First job: fix the date, then confirm the Harbour Hall hold still stands.\n\n**2. Confirm the 1:1 with Raj on Tuesday still makes sense.** It''s the only non-recurring commitment in your week, and the Aozora rebrand threads (logo shortlist, packaging, Arabic proofs) have been silent since late September — that''s the agenda: what happened while the thread went quiet.\n\n## P2 — Overdue, with dates that have already passed\n\n**3. Codeyard review request #63 — *[fernhill/website] Review requested: Aozora case study*, open since 11 Sep.** Nobody can merge it without you.\n\n**4. Dependabot: 4 security updates** on `fernhill/website`, from 14 Sep. Two months on a stale branch.\n\n**5. Money: settle September.** Sam''s *\"Receipts for September\"* (16 Sep), Ledgerline invoice `LL-2025111`, and a run of Konkan debits to reconcile against `Finance/2025/expenses.tsv`. Also check whether Linkroom''s Pro renewal actually hit on 3 October as it warned.\n\n## P3 — Hygiene that makes the rest trustworthy (30 minutes, once)\n\n**6. Do something with the 228 fake unread emails.** Until they''re gone, your unread badge is noise and you''ll never spot a real one.\n\n**7. Label the 75 newsletters.** Then `newsletter` stops 56 Kestrel editions from crowding anything that matters.\n\n**8. Check why mail has been silent since 26 September.** Seven weeks with zero real arrivals while a studio is actively billing clients is either a genuine lull or a broken filter. Worth ten minutes on filters and forwarding — this one is a *suspicion*, not a finding.\n\n---\n\n## Three things I want to be straight about\n\n- **I read no email bodies.** These items come from subjects, dates and threads. I can''t see whether #63 was reviewed inside Codeyard''s UI, or whether Sam''s receipts were paid by other means. Treat P2 as \"verify,\" not \"certainly undone.\"\n- **Your calendar is buried under fixtures.** Asking for \"this week\" across all calendars returned 100 events and nearly all were `Bulk NNN` filler on a **Bulk** calendar that''s marked *primary*, plus a **\"Daily forever\"** recurrence on Edge cases. I excluded both to find your six real events. Deleting those two calendars would make every future calendar question honest.\n- **Your colleagues aren''t in this workspace, but they''re on your domain.** `raj@`, `tomas@`, `priya@demo.trymetis.email` are invited to the **Monthly studio review on Mon 7 December, 14:00–15:00 UTC, Studio 1** — yet `listWorkspaceMembers` returns only you. So the workspace has one member while the studio works over the same domain.\n\n**Where I''d start:** block 30 minutes today to pick the Aozora launch date and email Mira about Harbour Hall — everything else can wait for Tuesday.\n\nWant me to draft that venue email to Mira Costa, or create the launch event once you''ve chosen a date? I can also clear the 228 fixtures and apply the newsletter label in two actions."}','assistant','v2','2026-11-22T04:33:04.991Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('7fcb71de-3044-4d2a-88cb-b3b5144d0ff1','a2157225-4dc1-4cde-986b-d827559a2ef5','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"text","text":"<turn sent-at=\"2026-11-22T04:33:07.123Z\" time-zone=\"UTC\" />","createdAt":1795321987132},{"type":"text","text":"Turn that to-do list into a short status update I could paste into chat.","createdAt":1795321987132}]}','user','v2','2026-11-22T04:33:07.170Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('3140a9c4-fc6b-47b2-8d6f-e675505b77c2','a2157225-4dc1-4cde-986b-d827559a2ef5','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"They want a short chat-pasteable status update from the to-do list. Should be plain, no markdown-heavy tables — chat-friendly. Short. No tools needed.\n\nKeep it brief: maybe 120-180 words. Use short lines, minimal formatting (maybe simple dashes, no headers heavy). Shouldn''t include caveats excessively but keep the honest note briefly? A status update for colleagues — shouldn''t include meta caveats about tooling. But maybe include \"verify\" hedges lightly.\n\nWrite it.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"They want a short chat-pasteable status update from the to-do list. Should be plain, no markdown-heavy tables — chat-friendly. Short. No tools needed.\n\nKeep it brief: maybe 120-180 words. Use short lines, minimal formatting (maybe simple dashes, no headers heavy). Shouldn''t include caveats excessively but keep the honest note briefly? A status update for colleagues — shouldn''t include meta caveats about tooling. But maybe include \"verify\" hedges lightly.\n\nWrite it."}],"createdAt":1795321987170},{"type":"text","text":"Here''s a version to paste:\n\n---\n\n**Status — week of 16 Nov**\n\nBack from Tokyo (returned today). Calendar is light: standups weekdays 09:00, 1:1 with Raj Tuesday 10:00. Everything below is what I''m chasing around that.\n\n**Priority this week**\n- **Aozora launch** — still undated. Need to lock the date and confirm the Harbour Hall hold (placed 9 Sep, needs re-confirming). This is the one thing with no calendar entry at all, so it''s first.\n- **Codeyard — Aozora case study (#63)** — review requested 11 Sep, still open, blocking merge.\n- **Dependabot** — 4 security updates pending on fernhill/website since mid-Sep.\n- **September close** — Sam''s receipts, Ledgerline LL-2025111, Konkan debits to reconcile; confirm the Linkroom Pro renewal went through on 3 Oct.\n\n**Housekeeping**\n- Clearing the fixture mail out of my inbox (unread count is meaningless right now) and labelling the newsletters.\n- Checking filters/forwarding — nothing real has landed since 26 Sep, which may just be a quiet stretch but I want to rule out a broken rule.\n\n**Also flagging:** Raj, Tomás and Priya are on the December studio review invite but aren''t workspace members — if we want them in here, that needs sorting.\n\nPing me if anything above should change order.\n\n---\n\nTwo notes on what I changed: I dropped the counts and tool-limitations talk (wrong audience for a chat update), and I softened \"overdue\" to \"verify\" items — since I haven''t read the mail bodies, I can''t tell whether #63 was reviewed inside Codeyard or Sam''s receipts were paid another way. Say the word if you''d rather it be blunter, or trimmed to just the P1.","createdAt":1795321987170}],"content":"Here''s a version to paste:\n\n---\n\n**Status — week of 16 Nov**\n\nBack from Tokyo (returned today). Calendar is light: standups weekdays 09:00, 1:1 with Raj Tuesday 10:00. Everything below is what I''m chasing around that.\n\n**Priority this week**\n- **Aozora launch** — still undated. Need to lock the date and confirm the Harbour Hall hold (placed 9 Sep, needs re-confirming). This is the one thing with no calendar entry at all, so it''s first.\n- **Codeyard — Aozora case study (#63)** — review requested 11 Sep, still open, blocking merge.\n- **Dependabot** — 4 security updates pending on fernhill/website since mid-Sep.\n- **September close** — Sam''s receipts, Ledgerline LL-2025111, Konkan debits to reconcile; confirm the Linkroom Pro renewal went through on 3 Oct.\n\n**Housekeeping**\n- Clearing the fixture mail out of my inbox (unread count is meaningless right now) and labelling the newsletters.\n- Checking filters/forwarding — nothing real has landed since 26 Sep, which may just be a quiet stretch but I want to rule out a broken rule.\n\n**Also flagging:** Raj, Tomás and Priya are on the December studio review invite but aren''t workspace members — if we want them in here, that needs sorting.\n\nPing me if anything above should change order.\n\n---\n\nTwo notes on what I changed: I dropped the counts and tool-limitations talk (wrong audience for a chat update), and I softened \"overdue\" to \"verify\" items — since I haven''t read the mail bodies, I can''t tell whether #63 was reviewed inside Codeyard or Sam''s receipts were paid another way. Say the word if you''d rather it be blunter, or trimmed to just the P1.","metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"}}','assistant','v2','2026-11-22T04:33:07.173Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
